# HCDE 530 Project Rules

This rule applies to all work in this repository.

## Directory structure (keep this section current)
```text
hcde530/
├── .cursorrules
├── .gitignore
└── HCDE 530 Week 2 Project/
    ├── README.md
    ├── PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
    ├── app_review_word_count.py
    ├── demo_dashboard.html
    ├── demo_responses.csv
    ├── demo_word_count.py
    ├── reviews.csv
    └── week2.md
```
- If files or folders are added, removed, or renamed, update this tree in the same change.
- Keep this map shallow and practical (main folders plus important project files).

## Project priorities
- Keep code beginner-friendly and well-structured for class assignments.
- Favor clarity and readable variable names over clever one-liners.
- Preserve existing file/folder names unless explicitly asked to rename.

## Python conventions
- Follow PEP 8 style and include short docstrings for non-trivial functions.
- Use `utf-8` encoding when reading text/CSV files.
- Handle missing fields or empty rows defensively when parsing data.
- Keep scripts runnable from their project folder with relative file paths.

## Data and analysis
- Never modify source CSV data unless explicitly requested.
- When adding analysis, include simple summary stats (count/min/max/average when relevant).
- Keep outputs reproducible and deterministic.

## HTML dashboard conventions
- Prefer a single standalone `.html` file (HTML/CSS/JS together) unless asked otherwise.
- Use plain JavaScript and avoid heavy dependencies.
- Build accessible markup: semantic headings, readable table labels, and clear button text.

## Workflow and safety
- Do not add secrets, tokens, or credentials to tracked files.
- Before finalizing changes, run quick sanity checks (script run or file open) when possible.
- If requirements are unclear, ask a concise clarifying question before major edits.
- Keep `.cursorrules` synchronized with the current project layout whenever edits change structure.